msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Fused Attention Example\n"
"\n"
"This example demonstrates how to use the fused attention operator in MindSpore. Fused attention combines multiple attention computation steps into a single operator, reducing memory overhead and improving computation efficiency.\n"
"\n"
"## Overview\n"
"\n"
"Fused attention is an optimized implementation of the attention mechanism. It fuses the computation of Query (Q), Key (K), and Value (V) matrices with the softmax operation, avoiding the need to materialize intermediate matrices in memory. This is particularly beneficial for long sequence inputs, as it significantly reduces memory usage.\n"
"\n"
"## Key Features\n"
"\n"
"- **Memory Efficiency**: By fusing operations, intermediate matrices are not stored in memory, reducing memory footprint.\n"
"- **Performance Improvement**: Reduces kernel launch overhead and improves computation speed.\n"
"- **Flexibility**: Supports various attention mask patterns and scaling factors.\n"
"\n"
"## Code Example\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import mindspore as ms\n"
"from mindspore import nn, ops\n"
"from mindspore.common.initializer import Normal\n"
"\n"
"class FusedAttention(nn.Cell):\n"
"    def __init__(self, hidden_size, num_heads, dropout_rate=0.1):\n"
"        super(FusedAttention, self).__init__()\n"
"        self.hidden_size = hidden_size\n"
"        self.num_heads = num_heads\n"
"        self.head_dim = hidden_size // num_heads\n"
"        self.dropout_rate = dropout_rate\n"
"\n"
"        # Linear projections for Q, K, V\n"
"        self.q_proj = nn.Dense(hidden_size, hidden_size, weight_init=Normal(0.02))\n"
"        self.k_proj = nn.Dense(hidden_size, hidden_size, weight_init=Normal(0.02))\n"
"        self.v_proj = nn.Dense(hidden_size, hidden_size, weight_init=Normal(0.02))\n"
"\n"
"        # Output projection\n"
"        self.out_proj = nn.Dense(hidden_size, hidden_size, weight_init=Normal(0.02))\n"
"\n"
"        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(p=dropout_rate)\n"
"        self.softmax = nn.Softmax(axis=-1)\n"
"\n"
"    def construct(self, query, key, value, mask=None):\n"
"        batch_size = query.shape[0]\n"
"\n"
"        # Project Q, K, V\n"
"        q = self.q_proj(query)\n"
"        k = self.k_proj(key)\n"
"        v = self.v_proj(value)\n"
"\n"
"        # Reshape to [batch_size, num_heads, seq_len, head_dim]\n"
"        q = q.view(batch_size, -1, self.num_heads, self.head_dim).transpose(0, 2, 1, 3)\n"
"        k = k.view(batch_size, -1, self.num_heads, self.head_dim).transpose(0, 2, 1, 3)\n"
"        v = v.view(batch_size, -1, self.num_heads, self.head_dim).transpose(0, 2, 1, 3)\n"
"\n"
"        # Compute attention scores\n"
"        scores = ops.matmul(q, k.transpose(0, 1, 3, 2)) / ms.Tensor(self.head_dim ** 0.5, ms.float32)\n"
"\n"
"        # Apply mask if provided\n"
"        if mask is not None:\n"
"            scores = scores.masked_fill(mask == 0, -1e9)\n"
"\n"
"        # Apply softmax and dropout\n"
"        attn_weights = self.softmax(scores)\n"
"        attn_weights = self.dropout(attn_weights)\n"
"\n"
"        # Compute output\n"
"        attn_output = ops.matmul(attn_weights, v)\n"
"        attn_output = attn_output.transpose(0, 2, 1, 3).view(batch_size, -1, self.hidden_size)\n"
"\n"
"        # Final projection\n"
"        output = self.out_proj(attn_output)\n"
"        return output\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Usage\n"
"\n"
"To use the fused attention module, instantiate it with the desired hidden size and number of heads, then call it with query, key, and value tensors:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"# Example usage\n"
"hidden_size = 768\n"
"num_heads = 12\n"
"batch_size = 2\n"
"seq_len = 128\n"
"\n"
"model = FusedAttention(hidden_size, num_heads)\n"
"query = ms.Tensor(np.random.randn(batch_size, seq_len, hidden_size), ms.float32)\n"
"key = ms.Tensor(np.random.randn(batch_size, seq_len, hidden_size), ms.float32)\n"
"value = ms.Tensor(np.random.randn(batch_size, seq_len, hidden_size), ms.float32)\n"
"\n"
"output = model(query, key, value)\n"
"print(output.shape)  # (2, 128, 768)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Performance Considerations\n"
"\n"
"- Fused attention is most beneficial when the sequence length is large, as it avoids the memory overhead of storing intermediate attention matrices.\n"
"- The operator is optimized for both GPU and Ascend hardware platforms.\n"
"- For best performance, ensure the head dimension is a multiple of 16 on Ascend hardware.\n"
"\n"
"## Conclusion\n"
"\n"
"Fused attention provides a memory-efficient and high-performance implementation of the attention mechanism. It is recommended for models with long sequences or when memory is a constraint.\n"

msgid "融合注意力（Fused Attention）"
msgstr "Fused Attention"

msgid "本节实现了一个基于 **Triton** 的 **Flash Attention v2 风格的融合注意力前向传播内核**，适用于昇腾（Ascend）NPU 平台。该实现支持："
msgstr "This section implements a **Triton**-based **Flash Attention v2-style fused attention forward propagation kernel**, suitable for the Ascend NPU platform. This implementation supports:"

msgid "**因果（causal）与非因果注意力**"
msgstr "**Causal and Non-Causal Attention**"

msgid "**分块计算（tiling）以处理长序列**"
msgstr "**Tiling to handle long sequences**"

msgid "**数值稳定性优化（max-shifted softmax）**"
msgstr "**Numerical Stability Optimization (max-shifted softmax)**"

msgid "整体结构包含两个核心 Triton 内核："
msgstr "The overall structure contains two core Triton kernels:"

msgid "`_attn_fwd_inner`：执行单个 query block 与 key/value blocks 的 attention 计算（分阶段处理 causal mask）"
msgstr "`_attn_fwd_inner`: Performs attention computation for a single query block against key/value blocks (handling the causal mask in stages)."

msgid "`_attn_fwd`：调度所有 query blocks，并管理 block 指针、accumulator 和归一化"
msgstr "`_attn_fwd`: schedules all query blocks and manages block pointers, accumulators, and normalization."

msgid "并通过 PyTorch `autograd.Function` 封装为可调用的 `attention` 函数，与 `torch_npu.npu_fusion_attention` 进行精度对齐验证。"
msgstr "The `attention` function is wrapped as a callable via PyTorch `autograd.Function` and validated for precision alignment with `torch_npu.npu_fusion_attention`."

